{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786518164,"nonce":"wWA3xBadzKPwcttAl5j+YSWMVxo=","title":"Six periodic handlers still loop every tenant inside one job execution — the fan-out half of cc0fac2's `Done when` is unbuilt","was":"**What is wrong.** cc0fac2 fixed `orgLister.Scopes`'s missing `deleted_at IS NULL` filter and made it page, but its own `Done when` had a second clause that never shipped: *\"the fan-outs that walk it enqueue per-tenant jobs instead of looping every tenant inside one handler.\"* Six job kinds still call `Scopes(ctx)` and loop the result synchronously inside a single job execution, exactly as before cc0fac2: `internal/app/workers.go:150` (`forEachOrg`, shared by `reapOccurrences`/`occurrence.reap`, `closeGroups`/`group.close`, `scoreFlaps`/`flap.score` — three job kinds off one loop), `:302` (`effectiveRetention`, called from `managePartitions`/`partitions.manage`), `:375` (`sweepDrills`, called from `pruneRetention`/`retention.prune`), and `internal/stats/worker/rollup.go:56` (`StatsRollup`/`stats.rollup`). That is `occurrence.reap`, `group.close`, `flap.score`, `partitions.manage`, `retention.prune` and `stats.rollup` — every one of them doing O(tenants) sequential work inside one execution, against one timeout, on one worker goroutine."}]}